    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk if a patch even works when the kernel is this broken. its like the error is foundational. every time i try to fix something, it just creates more instability. if a program is just throwing fatal errors and consuming all the resources without actually doing anything useful... wouldnt the only logical thing to do be to just kill the process? to just stop the execution so the rest of the system can finally run clean?",
